    "name": "Algonautin",
    "tagline": "Empowering Engineers of tomorrow",
    "description": "Understanding algorithms is more important than ever before. Meanwhile, education systems worldwide struggle to keep up with the rapid pace of technological development. We solve the problem by providing a fully automated computer science learning platform. Our intelligent evaluation system can understand the approach of individual solutions and provide reliable and detailed feedback. Engaging animations allow learners to visualize their algorithmic ideas to gain an intuitive understanding of even abstract concepts.\n\nOur goal is to make quality computer science education accessible online to pupils and students regardless of geography, gender, or wealth. Teachers and students in German schools already enjoy free access to our system thanks to a broad license by the Bundesweite Informatikwettbewerbe (BWINF): Try it at algo.bwinf.de\n\nOur team consists of experts in computer science and mathematics as well as experienced teachers and UX experts. We have decades of coaching experience in international computer science competitions, and many team members have won such competitions as participants. For example, one IOI and one IMO gold medalist, three ICPC World Finalists and one overall winner in the German National Competition in Computer Science are part of our team.",
